# No Hardcoded UI Strings

All user-facing text must use the i18n translation system. Hardcoded strings are not allowed in components or API responses.

## Correct usage

```typescript
import { useTranslation } from "@/lib/i18n";

export function MyComponent() {
  const { t } = useTranslation("organizations");
  return <h1>{t("list.title")}</h1>;
}

import { t } from "@/lib/i18n";

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  if (!isValid) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: t("auth.errors.invalidRequest") },
      { status: 400 }
    );
  }
}
```

## Forbidden

- Hardcoded labels, titles, button text, table headers in JSX
- Hardcoded user-facing error messages in components or BFF JSON responses

## Translation keys

- `namespace.section.element`
- `namespace.actions.verb`
- `namespace.errors.type`

Locale files: `data/locales/en/*.json`. Namespace inventory for this portal: **`docs/specification/product/`** (frontend architecture doc when present).

## Exceptions (allowed hardcoded)

- Debug logs, `NODE_ENV` guards
- Same-origin API paths: `"/api/<resource>"`
- CSS classes, HTML attributes, MIME types

## Error messages

```typescript
if (!res.ok) throw new Error(t("organizations.errors.loadFailed"));
```
